Bundled third-party software

The browser front end built by scripts/build-web.sh links the following into
web/dist/. Each is used unmodified and under its own licence.

CodeMirror 6 — @codemirror/state, @codemirror/view, @codemirror/language,
@codemirror/commands, @codemirror/lint, and their @lezer dependencies.
  Copyright (C) by Marijn Haverbeke and others
  MIT licence — https://codemirror.net/

esbuild is a build-time tool only and is not linked into the output.
  Copyright (C) Evan Wallace
  MIT licence — https://esbuild.github.io/

subset-font — the harfbuzz subsetter as WebAssembly, used at build time to
produce the math font below. Not linked into the output.
  Copyright (C) Andreas Lind
  BSD-3-Clause — https://github.com/papandreou/subset-font

web/dist/fonts/ carries **subsets** of STIX Two Math and STIX Two Text, built at
release time from the files scripts/fetch-font.sh obtains and verifies:

  stix-two-math-subset.woff2         the mathematics
  stix-two-text-subset.woff2         the prose
  stix-two-text-italic-subset.woff2  the prose, italic

Each is renamed, because a subset is a Modified Version under the licence and
because STIX Fonts is a trademark of the IEEE and these files are not what that
name refers to. The licence's Reserved Font Name, "TM Math", is not used.

  Copyright 2001-2021 The STIX Fonts Project Authors
  (https://github.com/stipub/stixfonts), with Reserved Font Name "TM Math".
  SIL Open Font License 1.1 — https://scripts.sil.org/OFL

  The licence text ships beside them as web/dist/fonts/OFL.txt — one licence for
  all three, since they are one release of one project — because the OFL
  requires it to travel with the bytes. `nomo html --embed-font` writes the same
  text into the document it embeds a font into, for the same reason.

The Rust crates compiled into the engine — libm and roxmltree — are each
MIT OR Apache-2.0. `cargo tree` lists them in full.

